## Overlay recovery and module presentation previews

The standalone helpers run in this workspace's prepared shell. `cse-build`
also delegates to them:

```bash
./cse-build login overlay --help
./cse-build login module-preview --check-only
```

`overlay apply --from /path/to/corrected-package-directory` updates the existing
workspace's complete package directory and inventory with a retained undo record.
`overlay edit --package NAME --environment COMPILER/LANE` supports local manual
editing with the same backup and validation. Both report potentially affected
locks; neither solves them automatically.

```bash
./cse-build login concretize --environment cce/common --reconcretize
./cse-build compute resume --environment cce/common
```

Use the recorded compiler/lane that actually failed. Reconcretize changes only
that selected lock and retains its previous bytes. Resume builds that environment
from its current lock and reuses installed matching hashes. It keeps module/view
generation separate. Other completed locks and installed prefixes remain intact.
Affected unselected locks are flagged before any later build against them.
The failed build succeeding with the correction is the verification; no additional
test program is required. See `pilots/cse-pilot/OVERLAY-RECOVERY.md` in Stack Content.

`module-preview --output /absolute/new/review-directory` generates from the
existing installed hashes into a separate Tcl module tree. Existing views must
already be present; this never solves, installs or publishes. Edit the saved
preview policies/presentation and pass them to a new iteration. Composer and
Spack upgrades are unnecessary when the existing module policy is valid. See
Stack Content's `pilots/cse-pilot/MODULE-PRESENTATION.md` for prerequisites,
older-launcher commands, alternative projections and clean-shell `module use`.
